&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT PROPRIETARY RESEARCH&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On our proprietary research team—Market Intelligence— you will uncover insights about companies, industries, and the broader economy through deep compliant fundamental research and applying data science and engineering techniques to alternative data sets. In partnership with our investment professionals and Compliance team, our team of analysts, data scientists and engineers work together to produce compliant research and build tools that inform our firm’s investments. We look for other bright, motivated, and collaborative people to join our team and grow with us—a majority of the leaders in our group were promoted from within.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Sector Analyst for European Equities, you will work with alternative data to gather industry context and business fundamentals. You will then partner with our team of data scientists and engineers to develop analyses that you’ll deliver as synthesized insights to our investment professionals to help aid in their research processes. The work is ever evolving, affording opportunities to tackle new challenges alongside research teammates from diverse backgrounds.&amp;nbsp;Specifically, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze and interpret alternative data from multiple sources and develop subject-matter expertise on the key themes and KPIs that drive the industry and companies within your assigned coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce research for internal consumption by our investment professionals across a variety of mediums, including written research reports, verbal communication, and visualization tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interact directly with our investment professionals to learn the discretionary investment process and help them to drive more informed investment decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with our proprietary research teams including Data Sourcing, Data Science, and Data Engineering, as well as Compliance, to source, evaluate, and draw value from new and existing data assets&amp;nbsp;to produce actionable research for investment professionals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT’S REQUIRED &amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An undergraduate or advanced degree with demonstrated academic success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;One to five years of prior equity/investment/scientific/industry research or consulting experience, including any relevant internship experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with technical coding/programming and ability to participate in a live technical screen (SQL, Python)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leveraging data analysis as part of the fundamental research process for business, public policy, finance, engineering, applied sciences, or other quantitative fields&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with analyzing novel data and explaining concepts to non-technical partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for finance, research, and using data to solve problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great organizational skills to handle a demanding workload, creativity, and a strong work ethic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate productively in a team environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to the highest ethical standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WE TAKE CARE OF OUR PEOPLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We invest in our people, their careers, their health, and their well-being. When you work here, we provide:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private Medical and Dental Insurances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous parental and family leave policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteer opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support for employee-led affinity groups representing women, people of colour and the LGBQT+ community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental and physical wellness programmes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition assistance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Non-contributory pension and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT POINT72&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Point72 is a leading global alternative investment firm led by Steven A. Cohen. Building on more than 30 years of investing experience, Point72 seeks to deliver superior returns for its investors through fundamental and systematic investing strategies across asset classes and geographies. We aim to attract and retain the industry’s brightest talent by cultivating an investor-led culture and committing to our people’s long-term growth. For more information, visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.point72.com/about&quot;&gt;www.Point72.com/about&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;A Career with Point72&#39;s Market Intelligence Team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On our proprietary research team—Market Intelligence—you’ll partner with our investment professionals and Compliance team to work with alternative data to uncover insights about companies, industries, and the broader economy through deep fundamental research and applying data science and engineering techniques. You’ll work alongside a talented team with diverse skills, backgrounds, and perspectives. Our sector data analysts, data scientists, data managers, and engineers work together to build compliant research products that are incorporated into the research process of our investment professionals. We look for other bright, motivated, and collaborative people to join our team and grow with us—a majority of the leaders in our group were promoted from within.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a forward-deployed solution architect: partner with EMEA Pods and business groups to identify high-value AI use cases, understand research workflows, and shape practical solution designs. Use lightweight proof-of-concepts selectively to validate value before larger build decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the bridge between EMEA teams and the firm’s AI resources: turn messy team signal into concrete product and platform asks, surface existing firm capabilities before teams reinvent them, and help firm-wide teams understand regional priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the enablement motion through teach-ins, prompt and tool literacy, and best-practice sharing, helping teams move beyond “AI is new and exciting” towards “AI is how we work.”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide the light-touch technical support that unblocks a team—such as a quick integration or precise bug report—without owning or maintaining core production systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track adoption and impact with simple metrics, and feed what is working back to the teams building firm-wide capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT&#39;S REQUIRED&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in a client-facing product, solution-engineering, or forward-deployed role. Early-stage or startup experience—working directly with users and moving quickly—is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A solid grasp of AI, solution design, and engineering best practices, with the judgement to assess feasibility and shape sound solutions. Comfort with Python, modern LLM and agentic tooling—including model APIs, retrieval-augmented generation, and agents—and SQL/data is expected; hands-on engineering experience is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s degree; a STEM background or equivalent hands-on experience is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of gathering requirements from non-technical users and translating them into solutions people actually adopt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine interest in financial markets and how investment research gets done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the confidence to work closely with senior investment professionals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product instinct, bias to action, high energy, and comfort operating with ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to the highest ethical standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WE TAKE CARE OF OUR PEOPLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We invest in our people, their careers, their health, and their well-being. When you work here, we provide:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private Medical and Dental Insurances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous parental and family leave policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteer opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support for employee-led affinity groups representing women, people of colour and the LGBQT+ community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental and physical wellness programmes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition assistance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Non-contributory pension and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT POINT72&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Point72 is a leading global alternative investment firm led by Steven A. Cohen. Building on more than 30 years of investing experience, Point72 seeks to deliver superior returns for its investors through fundamental and systematic investing strategies across asset classes and geographies. We aim to attract and retain the industry&#39;s brightest talent by cultivating an investor-led culture and committing to our people&#39;s long-term growth. For more information, visit https://point72.com/.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Weekly office requirement:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Hybrid&lt;strong&gt;: &lt;/strong&gt;Minimum 2 days a week&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employment type:&lt;/strong&gt; Permanent&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;At GWI we’re always looking for extraordinary people who thrive on making an extraordinary impact. Right now we’re looking for a Senior Account Executive to play a key role in our Enterprise team in London. If that’s you, and making a difference gets you out of bed in the morning, keep reading. It could be the start of something, well, extraordinary.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Sounds great, what will I be doing?&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our Senior Account Executive you’ll be reporting into the Director of Enterprise. Your primary focus will be to identify and sell our suite of products and services to enterprise organizations who are on a mission to understand their ever changing audiences and optimize their GTM strategy. GWI is on a mission to become the default human insight layer for AI systems to give decision makers in the world’s largest companies certainty.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;A few things you’ll be responsible for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;👉 Go high-and-wide within enterprise organizations to understand the full scope of the opportunity&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;👉 Work cross-functionally with our marketing, custom and strategic insights, solutions partners and product teams to deliver outstanding results&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;👉 &lt;strong&gt;Lead the entire new business sales cycle from initial opportunity creation to close&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;👉 Partner closely with your assigned Sales Development Representative (SDR) to strategize and execute on your outbound prospecting plan&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;👉 Establish and build credibility with your prospects from the outset. You’ll form a unique understanding of business challenges and present needs-based solutions that meet their business objectives!&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;👉 Track all sales activity, manage all sales opportunities and accurately forecast revenue achievement via Salesforce&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;👉 Develop your own territory plan and a pipeline that will fuel the ongoing growth of your business enabling you to exceed your quarterly and annual sales quota&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;It’s also fun; shaking things up is what working for GWI is all about. You’ll need to be flexible, comfortable with continuous change, and working in a high-tempo environment.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;🧳&amp;nbsp;What do I need to bring with me? 🧳&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll need to be able to demonstrate the core skills this role requires. You don&#39;t have to tick all the boxes right away; the important thing is that you’re willing to learn. Here’s what the team will be looking for in you:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;✔️ Follow MEDD(P)ICC sales methodology to qualify opportunities and progress deals through the pipeline&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;✔️ Experience of API based solutions&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;✔️ Proficient in leveraging AI tools to enhance day-to-day sales workflows, uncover insights, and create compelling client presentations and commercial materials&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;✔️ Sold to Enterprise sized clients (50k headcount and above)&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;✔️ Experience consistently closing deals &amp;gt;$100k ACV&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;✔️ Proven track-record of consistently meeting or over-achieving sales quotas&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;✔️ You are someone who takes ownership of their pipeline. Able to both execute your outbound strategy in collaboration with your SDR partner and with Marketing to close inbound leads.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Equally important is attitude. We want people who think big (to make an impact), ask why (to find a better way), and show respect (to everyone, at every level, all the time). Those are our values, and they’re a big part of what we’re looking for in you.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why GWI?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GWI is the human data layer that fuels decision-making and AI agents across the enterprise. In the age of AI, the way businesses consume insight is changing. Traditional research is no longer enough to keep up in a world of AI, automation, and agentic workflows. Our customers need insight, not just a platform, embedded directly into the tools and workflows they use every day. GWI has been at the forefront of this shift, through the launch of Agent Spark and by empowering decision makers to move with clarity, speed, and precision, grounding every action in real human understanding. GWI&#39;s mission remains the same: to help humans everywhere understand each other.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;🧘&amp;nbsp;What We Offer 🧘&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At GWI, you’ll find meaningful work, visible impact, and a culture that empowers you to do your best. Our package includes:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;🌱 Time to recharge – 25 days’ annual leave, plus office closures over the holidays.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;🌱 Health &amp;amp; wellbeing – Health cash plan, enhanced family benefits, carer days, and mental health support.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;🌱 Financial benefits – Competitive salary, 4% pension matching, and recognition programs that celebrate success.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;🌱 Flexibility &amp;amp; balance – Flexitime, early Friday finishes, hybrid and remote options, plus a “work from home” budget.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;🌱 Career growth – Accredited learning, leadership development, and global career mobility.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;🌱 Community &amp;amp; impact – DE&amp;amp;I initiatives, volunteering opportunities, donation matching, and payroll giving.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Put all that together and GWI is the friendliest, most fulfilling place any of us has ever worked.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;🫶&amp;nbsp;Diversity, Equity &amp;amp; Inclusion 🫶&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Diversity is fundamental to who we are—both as a data company and as a workplace. Our data reflects global realities, and so must our teams. We strive to ensure our workforce is as diverse and inclusive as the insights we provide to our clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Disability Confident employer, we welcome applications from disabled candidates and are committed to providing all necessary adjustments during the hiring process. We also actively encourage applications from underrepresented and marginalized communities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At GWI, you will find a place where you can contribute meaningfully, grow professionally, and belong fully.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;iframe src=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/embed/2g0akAyAlUU?si=dIgYyrKaAlNZK-NQ&quot; width=&quot;560&quot; height=&quot;314&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#li-hybrid&lt;br&gt;#LI-VS1&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every business is using AI. The ones that get it right start with real people. GWI is the human intelligence underneath: verified data that helps businesses understand what moves their audience, and act on it faster. If you want your work to matter, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;What will I be doing?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our Product Designer you’ll design how people and AI agents get to GWI data, working in a cross-functional squad alongside Product and Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Right now our biggest need is agentic, API and MCP. Customers reach GWI through agents, integrations and workflows as well as our platform, so you’ll shape the experiences built on our MCP servers and APIs: how a developer connects to an endpoint, how an agent calls a tool and gets a trustworthy answer, and how a person stays in control when it goes wrong. That’s where you’ll start, but there’s room to work in other squads and domains as our priorities change.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;A few things you’ll be responsible for:&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taking problems from discovery through to delivery, partnering with Product Managers, Engineers and Data teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing the experiences around our MCP servers and APIs (onboarding, authentication, tool and endpoint discovery, error handling, usage and permissions) and improving the workflows that take developers, analysts and AI agents to trusted data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing for agents and machines as well as people, working with Engineering on tools, schemas, naming and error messages so the machine-facing and human-facing sides feel like one product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using AI to speed up discovery, design and delivery, and prototyping with working code and live APIs so ideas get tested early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to our design system: proposing, designing and documenting components and patterns, including agentic and API-led ones, and working with Engineering to implement them consistently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to developer-facing content such as documentation, quickstarts and example flows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working at GWI means a high tempo environment where change is common. We’re building quickly because the industry is moving quickly, and our customers rely on us to stay ahead. If you like being part of that, you’ll enjoy it here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;What do I need to bring with me?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll need to be able to demonstrate the core skills this role requires. You don’t have to tick all the boxes right away; the important thing is that you’re willing to learn.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with AI tools: you use them to prototype quickly, ideally against live APIs or in code, as well as to speed up research and design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong design system knowledge: you’ve built or extended components and patterns, written usage guidance, and helped keep a product consistent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Some experience with API or MCP workflows, or agentic products (or a strong appetite to learn fast), and an understanding of how APIs work (REST, authentication, rate limits, schemas, errors) and how they shape the experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A solid product design and UX foundation, with a good grasp of interaction design and usability, and comfort in complex, technical product environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving and systems thinking: you break problems down, land on clear solutions, and see how a tool, an API response or an agent interaction fits into the wider journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication with technical and non-technical stakeholders, and a collaborative, proactive approach that makes the team around you better.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independence within your squad, the judgement to seek input on the more ambiguous challenges, and the curiosity to pick things up quickly and adapt when priorities change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Figma, FigJam and Jira, and experience using qualitative and quantitative insights to inform decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing developer tools, API documentation or developer portals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building MCP servers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data products, analytics or market research platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a design system that covers non-visual patterns, such as API error messaging, agent interaction states or developer documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of introducing a new process, tool or practice that your team adopted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running lightweight research with technical users, such as developers and data analysts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Why Join Us?&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on a problem few teams have solved: designing how AI agents and developers get to trusted data through our MCP servers and APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help set the patterns. You’ll shape how agentic and API-led experiences work at GWI and contribute to our design system, so your decisions carry across the product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Room to move. You’ll start in agentic, API and MCP, with the option to work in other squads and domains as our priorities change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hybrid setup, with 2 days a week in our London office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Weekly office requirement: 2 days&lt;br&gt;Employment type: Permanent&lt;br&gt;Seniority level: Intermediate to Senior&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Diversity, Equity &amp;amp; Inclusion 🫶&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Diversity is fundamental to who we are—as a data company and as a workplace. Our data reflects global realities, and so must our teams. We strive to build a workforce as diverse and inclusive as the insights we deliver.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Disability Confident employer, we welcome applications from disabled candidates and are committed to making adjustments throughout the hiring process—whether that&#39;s extra time, materials in advance or a different format, breaks, an adjusted interview format, assistive tools, or flexible scheduling. We&#39;re happy to discuss whatever would work best for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We actively encourage applications from underrepresented and marginalised communities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At GWI, you&#39;ll find a place to contribute meaningfully, grow professionally, and belong fully.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
